                "The third operational phase of the War Room executes the existential going concern assessment under ISA 570 (Revised) and FASB ASC Subtopic 205-40. The statutory evaluation horizon extends for exactly one year after the financial statement issuance date (March 1, 2026 to March 1, 2027 under US GAAP). The engagement team tests management's 12-month rolling cash flow forecast against debt maturity obligations, liquidity covenants, and operational expenditure commitments.",
                "Phase 1 Unmitigated Liquidity Stress and Covenant Default: The company holds $45,000,000 in unrestricted cash and $15,000,000 in undrawn credit facility lines ($60.0M total available liquidity). Forecast operating cash burn over the next twelve months is $80,000,000, and contractual debt principal repayments equal $25,000,000 ($105.0M total baseline cash outflows). Unmitigated cash runway is only 6.8 months, creating a baseline 12-month cash deficit of $45,000,000. Compounding this liquidity drain, audit testing of year-end syndicated debt covenants reveals a technical covenant breach: actual funded debt to EBITDA leverage is 4.62x against a maximum contractual covenant ceiling of 3.50x. Because the lending syndicate formally refused to execute a written twelve-month waiver, ASC Topic 470 mandates reclassifying $300,000,000 of long-term debt into CURRENT liabilities, instantly creating a $210M working capital deficit and raising presumptive substantial doubt in Phase 1.",
